  {
    "sha": "8cd4c91887ea361302dd6438ea00e6e745726a9b",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDhjZDRjOTE4ODdlYTM2MTMwMmRkNjQzOGVhMDBlNmU3NDU3MjZhOWI",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-13T07:48:27Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-13T07:48:27Z"
      },
      "message": "perf(adaptive): simplify growth outlines before opening\n\nThin each opening input at the existing 0.25 um arc tolerance to avoid\nrepeated offsets of the growth planner's fine join vertices. Use an\nexplicit stack, retain the original outline when normalization changes\nits loop or hole counts, and clip every opened result to its original\nregion after a 0.51 um extra erosion.\n\nKeep all load, crossing, kink and geometry-budget laws unchanged. Pin\nwhole-region containment on narrow and nested outlines, bound charged\ngrowth vertices on a fine rounded slot, and remeasure the adaptive\nfixtures and the actual STEP bore in release and debug. Record the\nmeasured Linux path triple and the unmeasured platform limitation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-6 Astra) <noreply@openai.com>\n\nFixes #882",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "4c9acef22f2f53e81bc8dccee3a31d93c52e114f",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NeoTech/Camcraft/git/trees/4c9acef22f2f53e81bc8dccee3a31d93c52e114f"
