      },
      "message": "docs(adaptive): name the inset as the containment guard; macOS bore triple\n\nThe PR #1376 review's mutation checks showed the extra erosion INSET,\nnot the intersection with the original region, keeps the opening\ninside its source: eroding by rho + INSET and dilating by rho cannot\ncross a wall, island, hole, notch or the seam while Douglas-Peucker\nstays within SIMPLIFY of the original. Reword rings.rs, simplify.rs\nand the decision record to say so, with the intersection and the\nloop/hole-count fallback as extra protection, and pin\nINSET > SIMPLIFY + ARC_TOL with a unit test.\n\nUpdate the macOS arm of the bore pin to (16026, 15382, 1413), measured\non Apple silicon in release at 8cd4c918.\n\nRefs #882\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
